-- title:
--   Transversal floor prime at elliptic j-values; horizontal unramifiedness elsewhere
-- statement:
--   Let $q \geq 5$ be a prime, let $M' \geq 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the $L$-subextension of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and let $K_0 \leq K$ be the analogous $L$-subextension generated by the field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$, acting compatibly on $K$ and $K_0$; let $j \in K$ and $j_0 \in K_0$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent series are the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$. Write $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ (resp. of $A[j_0]$ in $K_0$), and $\iota$ for a ring map between these two compatible with the inclusion $K_0 \leq K$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite and infinite chart algebras. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which $f\,y = x$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$ at which the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ mapping to $z$ whose prime is maximal. Assume given an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring map $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, such that $\varphi(j) \notin \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has a nonzero $q$-torsion point, and such that $\varphi(j) = 0$ or $\varphi(j) = 1728$; assume also that every element of the finite chart algebra which is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in the prime of $y$. Then, viewing the upper finite chart algebra as an algebra over the floor one via $\iota$, there is a prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}_0$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0\,j_0$ such that $\mathfrak{Q}_0$ is contained in the contraction along $\iota$ of the prime of $y$, the image of $\varpi$ does not lie in $\mathfrak{Q}_0$, in every localisation $O$ of the floor chart algebra at that contracted prime the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{Q}_0$ together with the image of $\varpi$ is the maximal ideal of $O$, and for every prime $\mathfrak{Q}$ of the upper finite chart algebra with $\mathfrak{Q}$ contained in the prime of $y$, of height $1$, not containing the image of $\varpi$, and with contraction along $\iota$ different from $\mathfrak{Q}_0$, the upper chart algebra is unramified at $\mathfrak{Q}$ over the floor chart algebra.
--
--   This is the local comparison, at a closed point of the special fibre over $q$ lying on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions, between the integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ and that of the floor $X_0(M')$, at a point whose $j$-value is ordinary and equal to $0$ or $1728$: a single horizontal prime of the floor passes through the point transversally to the fibre, and along all other horizontal primes of height one through the point the covering is unramified. It feeds the regularity statement for the fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ at such a point.
